course: dictionary
lesson: 1476
title: Catchy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A catchy tune, song or slogan is easy to remember, and it stays in your head after you hear it. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it. «A slogan is a short catchy phrase» tells you that a slogan is short and easy to remember.
explain: Catchy can also describe a name or idea that grabs your attention. This is an informal use, so people say it when talking, not in formal writing. Look at the clues: «The hook is the catchiest bit of a song, often in the chorus» tells you the hook is the part you remember most.
explain: Catchy can change its form to compare things. Catchier means more catchy, and catchiest means the most catchy. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you probably have it right.
fact: Catchy means easy to remember and stays in your head.
fact: Catchy can also describe a name or idea that grabs attention; this is an informal use.
fact: The comparison forms are catchier (more catchy) and catchiest (the most catchy).
fact: «A slogan is a short catchy phrase.»
fact: Adverts use catchy slogans and jingles to help you remember a product.
exercise: «A slogan is a short catchy phrase.» What does catchy mean in this sentence? | *Easy to remember | Very long and boring | Written in red ink | Hard to read
exercise: «The hook is the catchiest bit of a song, often in the chorus.» Find and copy the word that means the most catchy. | song | *catchiest | chorus | bit
exercise: Before an election, adverts use «catchy slogans» to get noticed. Why do they use catchy slogans? | So people never read it | So the advert is very long | So people fall asleep during the advert | *So people remember the product
test: Ben says the name «Blizzard Bananas» is catchy. What does he mean? | It is cold and icy | *It grabs attention and is easy to remember | It is a boring name | It is written in a language nobody knows
test: «Kind truths often mix three things.» One example says, «the chorus is catchy, the drums need work, want to practise?» What is the first thing this kind truth notices? | *The chorus is catchy | Want to practise | The drums need work | Nothing is good about the song
exam: The band's new song is so ___ that I hum it all day. | quiet | boring | slow | *catchy
